From: Herman Brule <brule.herman@confiared.com>
Subject: firewall4: a source-MAC match on a device without an Ethernet header

nft compiles `ether saddr` with an implicit `meta iiftype ether`, so on a
PPPoE WAN (pppoe-wan, ARPHRD_PPP) a rule or redirect with src_mac never
matched: a DHCPv6 reply allowed by its source MAC was rejected and the WAN
had no IPv6. Each such rule is also emitted without the MAC, restricted to
devices without an Ethernet header (`meta iiftype != ether`), where it
applies on its other matches.

--- a/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/mangle-rule.uc
+++ b/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/mangle-rule.uc
@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@
 	ether saddr {{ fw4.set(rule.smacs_pos) }} {%+ endif -%}
 {%+ if (rule.smacs_neg): -%}
 	ether saddr != {{ fw4.set(rule.smacs_neg) }} {%+ endif -%}
+{%+ if (rule.no_ether): -%}
+	meta iiftype != ether {%+ endif -%}
 {%+ if (rule.icmp_types): -%}
 	{{ (rule.family == 4) ? "icmp" : "icmpv6" }} type {{ fw4.set(rule.icmp_types) }} {%+ endif -%}
 {%+ if (rule.icmp_codes): -%}
